    <body>
      <div xml:id="gom-sir5">
        <head xml:id="gom-sir5-Hd1e98">Caput 5</head>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir5-Dd1e100">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir5-Hd1e102">Versus 11</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir5-d1e104">
            <pb ed="#P" n="1190C"/>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir5-Qd1e108" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir5_11@1-3">Non ventiles te,</quote>
            etc.
            <ref xml:id="gom-sir5-Rd1e111"><name xml:id="gom-sir5-Nd1e112" ref="#RabanusMaurus">RAB.</name></ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir5-Qd1e115"><seg type="qs">Levitatem reprehendit</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">duplicitas doctrinae eorum, in qua modo vera, modo falsa proferunt, peccatores esse ostendit.</seg></quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-sir5-Dd1e124">
          <head xml:id="gom-sir5-Hd1e126">Versus 13</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-sir5-d1e128">
            <quote xml:id="gom-sir5-Qd1e130" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/sir5_13@1-2">Esto mansuetus.</quote>
            Bonum est mansuete audire, et suscipere verbum veritatis, et modeste ac prudenter proferre; unde: <quote xml:id="gom-sir5-Qd1e133" source="http://scta.info/resource/iac1_19@5-19">Sit omnis homo velox ad audiendum, tardus ad loquendum et tardus ad iram.</quote>. Et paulo post: <quote xml:id="gom-sir5-Qd1e136" source="http://scta.info/resource/iac1_21@9-18">In mansuetudine suscipite insitum verbum, quod potest salvare animas vestras</quote><ref xml:id="gom-sir5-Rd1e138"><name xml:id="gom-sir5-Nd1e139" ref="#RabanusMaurus">Ibid.</name></ref><!-- check: attribution inside gloss body --> In Proverbiis quoque dicitur: <quote xml:id="gom-sir5-Qd1e143" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov29_20@1-12">Vidisti hominem velocem ad loquendum? stultitia magis speranda est, quam correctio illius</quote>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
